=20

I write further to my urgent filing today of an ACO-compliant N461 Judicial=
 Review bundle in Zahmoul v Ministry of Justice & HMCTS, and to my email to =
Case Progression requesting a case reference number.

=20

I have been informed that no assistance can be provided by Case Progression=
 until a case reference number has been allocated, and that I must therefore=
 contact the General Office.

=20

Accordingly, I respectfully request that:
A case reference number for my N461 Judicial Review claim be allocated as a=
 matter of urgency; and
Confirmation be provided that my N461 bundle (sent today under the subject =
line =E2=80=9CN461 Urgent Bundle =E2=80=93 Zahmoul v MoJ & HMCTS=E2=80=9D) has been received a=
nd accepted for issue.
=20

This matter is medically urgent. My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has=
 provided a signed report confirming that I am in a clinically fragile psych=
iatric state and that delay in the Court process creates a significant safeg=
uarding risk. I am a disabled litigant (Autism and PTSD), and the Court=E2=80=99s =
duties under the Equality Act 2010 and the Public Sector Equality Duty (s.14=
9) are therefore engaged.

=20

I am acting as a litigant in person and do not have the financial means to =
obtain legal representation. I have done everything I can to comply with the=
 Administrative Court=E2=80=99s requirements and to provide a single, court-ready =
N461 bundle.

=20

For these reasons, I would be very grateful if a case reference number coul=
d be issued today, and if my claim could then be progressed to case progress=
ion for urgent consideration alongside my N463 application.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: Nadia@rosekross.com

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

From: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Date: Friday, November 28, 2025 at 7:32=E2=80=AFAM
To: Administrative Court Office Immediates <administrativecourtoffice.immed=
iates@justice.gov.uk>
Cc: "Administrative Court Office, List Office" <administrativecourtoffice.l=
istoffice@justice.gov.uk>
Subject: Re: URGENT: Filing of N461 Judicial Review Bundle =E2=80=94 Request for =
Immediate Sealing & Judicial Consideration

=20

Dear Administrative Court,

Further to your email requesting an ACO-compliant single-PDF bundle, I now =
resubmit the entire Judicial Review application in one consolidated document=
:

=20

Attachment: N461 Urgent Bundle =E2=80=93 28 November 2025 (single PDF)

=20

This document contains:
N461 Claim Form (with continuation sheets)
Detailed Statement of Facts
Detailed Grounds
Witness Statement and Exhibits
Draft Order
Signed medical evidence from my treating physician, Dr. Bruce Hayse
All supporting materials in the correct order
=20

I confirm that this is a single, unified, ACO-compliant PDF as requested.

1. Medical Emergency =E2=80=94 Urgent Judicial Action Required Today

=20

My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has submitted a signed clinical repo=
rt (included within the PDF bundle) confirming:
I am currently in a severe psychiatric crisis
My stability depends on timely judicial action
Any delay significantly increases the risk of hospitalisation
The matter must be treated as urgent for safeguarding reasons
=20

This places the Court under statutory duties engaged by:
Equality Act 2010, ss.20=E2=80=9321 (reasonable adjustments)
Equality Act 2010, s.149 (Public Sector Equality Duty)
The overriding objective, particularly protections for vulnerable litigants
Administrative Court disability guidance
=20

Given the seriousness of my condition, I respectfully request sealing and j=
udicial consideration today.

=20

Waiting until Monday would contradict the medical evidence and expose me to=
 significant and documented clinical risk.

=20

2. I am a litigant in person with no access to legal representation

=20

I respectfully reiterate that I cannot obtain legal advice due to financial=
 constraints.

Your request that I =E2=80=9Cseek legal advice=E2=80=9D cannot act as a barrier to my r=
ight to access the Administrative Court.

=20

I have now:
Complied fully with PD 54A
Provided the N461
Provided the N463
Filed every required continuation sheet
Assembled the bundle exactly as requested, in one coherent PDF
Served the Defendants
Provided urgent medical evidence
=20

3. Request for Immediate Action

=20

Given:
the medically urgent situation,
the ACO-compliant bundle now filed,
the fact that the N463 has been pending since 25 November,
and the statutory duties engaged,
=20

I respectfully request:

=20

(1) Sealing of the N461 today

=20

(2) Immediate referral of the N463 to a judge today

=20

(3) Confirmation of urgent listing

=20

I would be grateful for written confirmation of receipt, acceptance, and se=
aling.

=20

Thank you for your attention to this urgent and medically fragile matter.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

From: Administrative Court Office Immediates <administrativecourtoffice.imm=
ediates@justice.gov.uk>
Date: Friday, November 28, 2025 at 7:06=E2=80=AFAM
To: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Subject: Re: URGENT: Filing of N461 Judicial Review Bundle =E2=80=94 Request for =
Immediate Sealing & Judicial Consideration

=20

Good afternoon,

=20

Please note an ACO compliant bundle must be filed as soon as possible: Admi=
nistrative Court: Information for Court Users =E2=80=93 June 2022 - Courts and Tri=
bunals Judiciary

=20

Please see guidance attached https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/20=
22/07/Administrative-Court-Information-for-court-users-June22.pdf)

=20

The court cannot accept your application and supporting documents in separa=
ted documents and multiple emails.

=20

Please resubmit and ensure all key supporting documents are available for r=
eview.

=20

=20

Kind regards,

S Sikity**OFFICIAL**

Administrative Court Office | Issues and Enquiries

=20

King's Bench Division | HMCTS | Royal Courts of Justice| Strand, London | W=
C2A 2LL

Phone: 020 7947 6000

Web: www.gov.uk/hmcts

PLEASE DO NOT SEND EMAILS TO PERSONAL INBOXES AS NO ACTION WILL BE TAKEN. P=
ERSONAL INBOXES ARE NOT MONITORED. PLEASE SEND ALL EMAILS TO :

administrativecourtoffice.generaloffice@justice.gov.uk


Daily Cause List: http://www.justice.gov.uk/courts/court-lists/list-rcj
Listing Enquiries: listoffice@administrativecourtoffice.justice.gov.uk

General Enquiries: generaloffice@administrativecourtoffice.justice.gov.uk

Criminal & Extradition Enquiries: crimex@administrativecourtoffice.justice.=
gov.uk

Skeleton Arguments: london.skeletonarguments@administrativecourtoffice.just=
ice.gov.uk

=20

For information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see: https=
://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about=
/personal-information-charter

=20

In accordance with Practice Direction 5B - Electronic communication and fil=
ing we ask you to do the following when sending an e-mail message to the cou=
rt:
Clearly state the Court's action number, parties=E2=80=99 names and any dates rel=
ating to an up-coming hearing in the subject header.
In accordance with Practice Direction 3.3a, please do not submit documents =
which carry a payable fee; such e-mails will be deleted.
We do not accept documents over 50 pages by electronic means.
=20

=20

From: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Sent: Friday, November 28, 2025 1:31 PM
To: Administrative Court Office Immediates <administrativecourtoffice.immed=
iates@justice.gov.uk>
Subject: URGENT: Filing of N461 Judicial Review Bundle =E2=80=94 Request for Imme=
diate Sealing & Judicial Consideration=20

=20

=20

Dear Administrative Court,

=20

I write as a litigant in person without access to legal representation, and=
 in extremely urgent medical circumstances, to file the complete N461 Judici=
al Review bundle as directed.

=20

Please find attached:

=20

1. N461 Claim Form (with continuation sheets)

2. Full N461 Bundle =E2=80=94 including Detailed Grounds, WS, and exhibits

3. Signed medical report from Dr Bruce Hayse confirming clinical crisis and=
 the need for urgent judicial intervention

=20

1. Why this must be sealed and listed today

=20

Your earlier emails indicated that an N463 cannot be considered unless acco=
mpanied by a full N461.

I have now complied fully and precisely with the requirements of PD 54A.

=20

Given that:
the N463 urgent application was filed on 25 November,
the Defendants have been properly served,
and the full N461 bundle is now filed,
=20

I respectfully request that the claim be sealed today and immediately place=
d before a judge for urgent consideration pursuant to:
PD 54A,
s.31A Senior Courts Act,
and the overriding objective, particularly for vulnerable court users.
=20

=20
2. Medical urgency =E2=80=94 exceptional vulnerability (clinical evidence attache=
d)
=20

My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has issued a signed medical report c=
onfirming:

I am in a severe state of psychiatric risk,

=20
my stability depends on the certainty and timing of the Court=E2=80=99s process,
and that this matter must be expedited for safeguarding reasons,
and he specifically warns that hospitalisation may be required absent timel=
y judicial action.
=20

This must be treated as exceptional vulnerability under:
the Equality Act 2010,
the Public Sector Equality Duty,
and the Court=E2=80=99s duty to provide reasonable adjustments.
=20

=20

3. I am a litigant in person =E2=80=94 I cannot afford legal advice

=20

Your previous message stated:

=E2=80=9CPlease seek legal advice.=E2=80=9D

=20

I wish to clarify respectfully that:

=20
I do not have the financial means to obtain legal representation;
I am acting entirely as a litigant in person;
and the Administrative Court Guide expressly anticipates, and protects, LiP=
s;
the requirement to =E2=80=9Cseek legal advice=E2=80=9D cannot be a condition of access =
to the Court.
=20

I have now followed every procedural instruction and provided the materials=
 the Court indicated were required.

=20

4. Request

=20

In light of:
the urgent medical evidence,
the statutory disability duties owed,
the fact that all procedural documents are now filed,
and the fact that the N463 urgent application has been pending for three da=
ys,
=20

I respectfully request that the Court:

=20

(1) Seal the N461 claim today

=20

(2) Refer the N463 to a judge immediately, today

=20

(3) Confirm listing for an urgent oral consideration

=20

(as requested in Section 3 of N463)

=20

Please confirm receipt and sealing at your earliest opportunity.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: Nadia@rosekross.com

=20

